<ContentPage
  title="A place to stay during the Nijmegen Four Days Marches — Vierdaagse Logeren"
  description="Planning to walk the Four Days Marches from abroad? Here's what you need to know about finding a place to stay in Nijmegen — early, and without the stress."
  locale="en"
  h1="A place to stay during the Nijmegen Four Days Marches"
>
  <p>
    Coming from outside the Netherlands for the Vierdaagse — the Nijmegen Four Days
    Marches? You're not alone: thousands of international walkers make the trip every
    year. One thing catches many of them off guard: Nijmegen is a small city, and
    accommodation fills up fast.
  </p>

  <h2>Book earlier than you think</h2>
  <p>
    If you're already arranging flights and time off work, add your accommodation
    search to that same timeline. Campsites and central hotels are typically the first
    to sell out — often months before the event, not weeks.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to look</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Nijmegen itself — closest to the start/finish, most in demand, first to fill up</li>
    <li>Surrounding towns (Wijchen, Groesbeek, Cuijk, and others along the route) — more availability, still a manageable travel distance</li>
    <li>Local/private options — some residents offer a room, garden, or driveway for walkers during the event</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to expect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices rise as the event gets closer — booking early saves money, not just stress</li>
    <li>English is widely spoken in Nijmegen, but don't expect every small campsite or private host to have an English-language listing — a short, polite message usually works fine</li>
    <li>Public transport and cycling infrastructure make towns further from the centre more workable than they might seem on a map</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick checklist</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Check this year's official Four Days Marches dates as soon as they're announced</li>
    <li>Decide how central you want to be versus how much you want to spend</li>
    <li>
      Compare <a href="/en/camping">camping</a>,
      <a href="/en/particuliere-verhuur">private stays</a>, and
      <a href="/en/hotels-bb">hotels &amp; B&amp;Bs</a>
    </li>
    <li>Book as soon as something fits — don't wait for a "better" deal that likely won't come</li>
  </ol>
</ContentPage>
